DISCUSSION = [
    "The principal contribution of this study is a framework that measures AID-driven mutation from whatever a "
    "platform delivers, reads or chromatograms, and replaces the two assumptions that make low-frequency calling from "
    "single reads unreliable for SHM. Instead of trusting quality scores, SHMtrace measures the background in the "
    "AID-null libraries that SHM studies already include, at the level of substitution type, strand, and base quality, "
    "and it checks this calibration by holding out each control in turn. Instead of treating reads as replicates, it "
    "tests animals. A quality-based caller either missed most true mutations in nanopore reads or, when made "
    "permissive, called as much background as the uncorrected rule, and pooling reads produced false positives in more "
    "than 90% of simulated experiments without a true difference.",
    "Comparator performance depends on the assay and operating range. LoFreq was designed for deep short-read data "
    "with calibrated qualities; its base-alignment correction suppressed nearly all nanopore calls here, and disabling "
    "it still limited recovery of low-support variants. This is not a defect of LoFreq on its intended data: a "
    "per-base error model fitted without matched controls has no way to reach this assay's library-specific "
    "background. Above Q40, measured control error stopped decreasing and varied between runs ({q40_lo}–{q40_hi} × "
    "10^{−5}; Figure S2), supporting empirical assessment of background. ClairS and DeepSomatic recovered clean "
    "variants at higher allele fractions but few real SHM calls; chemistry/model mismatches further qualify "
    "external-data comparisons. Germline callers were expected to miss rare variants. Geneious provided greater "
    "single-read recall on J_{H}4 and *Pim1* but more false calls on each amplicon. Unresolved single-read events can "
    "instead be estimated in aggregate. Sensitive mode increases the empirical target to 0.20: single-read recall "
    "reached {sens_jh4_1}% on J_{H}4 and {sens_n114_1}% on N114 V_{H}, with observed FDR {sens_jh4_fdr} and {sens_n114_fdr}. "
    "These trade-offs should guide settings according to the experimental question.",
    "What each platform contributes to an SHM experiment differs, and SHMtrace reads all four. A Sanger clone is one "
    "molecule read once, so its mutations are read directly. There is no read support to weigh against a background, "
    "and so nothing for a per-call test to work on: the AID-null clones measure a background reported beside the "
    "counts instead, and how much of each animal’s total it explains. Nanopore and Illumina libraries carry matched "
    "AID-null arms, so each candidate is tested against the errors those controls make: nanopore spans the whole "
    "amplicon, making the 3′ decline visible without tiling, identifying clones from the V(D)J junction and ordering "
    "their mutations into a tree, while Illumina gives depth without that linkage. PacBio combines length with "
    "per-base accuracy, used here on class-switch junctions; that deposit carries no AID-null arm, so it is "
    "reported without control-calibrated calls. Figure S20 sets out what each measured; the "
    "Sanger re-analysis also exposed bookkeeping problems that SHMtrace now checks explicitly.",
    "Published sequence collections can support reproducible reanalysis when clones are linked to animals and "
    "genotypes. SHMtrace recovered the principal J_{H}4 frequency and G:C comparisons and closely matched SW_{HEL} "
    "counts across five arms and twelve substitution types. Agreement was incomplete: Wt frequencies differed after "
    "denominator harmonization, the published *Mkln1* A:T decrease was not significant in the reanalysis, and the "
    "SW_{HEL} total-mutation inference differed under a different test (Tables S4 and S5; Figures S13–S15). Deposits "
    "should therefore include explicit clone-to-animal assignments and original counting conventions, alongside "
    "sequences and chromatograms.",
    "Read accounting, fixed-seed sampling and a shared desktop/command-line engine support routine use. The power "
    "analysis also illustrates the importance of biological replication: how many animals a study needs depends on "
    "the difference it seeks. Under variation estimated from three Wt J_{H}4 mice, the AID-competent against "
    "AID-null contrasts made here separate at three animals per group, whereas a two-fold difference between two "
    "AID-proficient groups would require approximately twenty, with considerable uncertainty in that estimate "
    "(Figure S7B). Increasing sequencing depth cannot substitute for independent biological samples.",
]
LIMITATIONS = [
    "SHMtrace relies on representative AID-null controls prepared and sequenced alongside the samples. Error profiles "
    "can vary between runs and basecalling configurations, and calibration using controls from a different run was not "
    "evaluated. With one nanopore run per assay, the present results do not establish performance across independent "
    "runs.",
    "The reported variants remain subject to technical uncertainty. Without UMIs, early PCR errors, recombination and "
    "repeated sequencing of PCR-derived molecules cannot be reliably distinguished from genuine mutations or expanded "
    "biological lineages. Mutation trees therefore describe relationships among reads rather than independently "
    "established cellular lineages. The default ≥50% allele-frequency filter can also remove genuine mutations shared "
    "by a dominant lineage. Excluded sites are reported for review, and experiments with a known starting sequence can "
    "use an optional reference policy that retains high-frequency differences. Single-read mutations that cannot be "
    "called individually are estimated only in aggregate, and unique-variant densities require comparison at matched "
    "sequencing depth.",
    "The empirical false-discovery estimate depends on the available controls and can exceed its nominal target when "
    "background differs between libraries. Noisy-control exclusion requires at least three controls, and its effect "
    "should be reviewed. Sample-specific artifacts absent from the controls may still pass the test; spectrum and "
    "clustering flags can identify unusual patterns but require interpretation. At weakly mutated targets such as "
    "Pim1, signal remained close to background.",
    "The core validation used three animals per group for J_{H}4 and one locus per cell system. Settings were "
    "developed using these libraries and applied to public datasets without dataset-specific retuning, although the "
    "noisy-control exclusion rule was introduced after inspection of the Ramos results. Evaluation on an independent "
    "sequencing run with new biological samples would provide a stronger test of generalizability. Indel validation "
    "comprised nanopore spike-ins and one Illumina biological phenotype, while UMI validation used rRNA rather than "
    "SHM data. These experiments do not establish performance on biological nanopore indels or UMI-tagged SHM "
    "libraries; molecule-level consensus remains preferable when available. Two Sanger studies originated from the "
    "authors’ laboratory, while the independent Sanger study provided sequences without chromatograms or AID-null "
    "controls. Together, these datasets evaluate distinct parts of the workflow, with different limits on the "
    "conclusions each can support.",
]

